{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "description": "Registry of named scenarios built on top of a base model.",
  "properties": {
    "scenarios": {
      "additionalProperties": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/d_1aa28628f45df66f024e"
      },
      "description": "Map of scenario name → definition.",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "scenarios"
  ],
  "title": "ScenarioSet",
  "type": "object",
  "$id": "https://finstack_quant.dev/schemas/statements_analytics/1/scenario_set.schema.json",
  "$defs": {
    "d_08ce974392238bd9f951": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Parameters of [`ForecastSpec::Seasonal`].",
      "properties": {
        "growth": {
          "description": "Trend growth per period as a decimal: 0.03 = 3%; defaults to none.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "historical": {
          "description": "Observations in the line's base units, oldest first; at least two full cycles.",
          "items": {
            "format": "double",
            "type": "number"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "max": {
          "description": "Upper bound clamped onto generated values, in the line's base units.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "min": {
          "description": "Lower bound clamped onto generated values, in the line's base units.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "mode": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/d_37bdaa203daeacc7cf76",
          "description": "How the seasonal pattern combines with the trend."
        },
        "season_length": {
          "description": "Periods per seasonal cycle.",
          "format": "uint64",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "historical",
        "season_length",
        "mode"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "d_1aa28628f45df66f024e": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Definition for a single named scenario.\n\nScenarios are attached to a base [`FinancialModelSpec`] and specify an\noptional parent plus typed scalar or monetary value overrides and forecast\nspecification overrides for named nodes.\n\nThe JSON representation mirrors the design docs example:\n\n```json\n\"downside\": {\n  \"parent\": \"base\",\n  \"overrides\": { \"revenue_growth\": -0.05, \"margin\": -0.02 }\n}\n```",
      "properties": {
        "forecast_overrides": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/d_8ed123e8acaef4d5eee1"
          },
          "description": "Forecast overrides for model nodes, keyed by `node_id`.\n\nEach entry replaces the node's whole [`ForecastSpec`] in this scenario:\nthe method and every parameter it reads (growth rates, `curve`\npaths, `seed`, `std_dev` and other stochastic parameters, external\n`series`, `min` / `max` bounds). A node without a forecast gains one.\nAcross a parent chain the child's spec replaces the parent's for the\nsame node. Parameters are validated when the scenario is evaluated.\n\nThe forecast fills forecast periods only, and explicit values still\nwin (`Value > Forecast > Formula`): a value override, a per-period\noverride or a model value in a forecast period hides the forecast in\nthat period.",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "overrides": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/d_39fe593d8e226e27da6a"
          },
          "description": "Typed overrides for model nodes.\n\nOverrides apply to forecast periods only and must match the target\nnode's scalar or monetary type and currency.",
          "type": "object"
        },
        "parent": {
          "description": "Optional parent scenario to inherit overrides from.\n\nParent chains can be arbitrarily deep but must be acyclic. Later\nscenarios in the chain override earlier ones for the same `node_id`.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "period_overrides": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "additionalProperties": {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/d_39fe593d8e226e27da6a"
            },
            "type": "object"
          },
          "description": "Typed per-period overrides for model nodes, keyed `node_id` then\nperiod id.\n\nA per-period override applies only to the named forecast period and\ntakes precedence over a model-wide `overrides` entry for the same node\nin that period. Across a parent chain the child's per-period value wins\nfor that (node, period), but a child's model-wide override does not\nclear a parent's per-period overrides for other periods.",
          "type": "object"
        }
      },
      "type": "object"
    },
    "d_1b5f98440d110c152454": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Parameters of [`ForecastSpec::GrowthPct`].",
      "properties": {
        "max": {
          "description": "Upper bound clamped onto generated values, in the line's base units.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "min": {
          "description": "Lower bound clamped onto generated values, in the line's base units.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "rate": {
          "description": "Growth per period as a decimal: 0.03 = 3%.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "start": {
          "description": "Level at the opening of the forecast suffix, in the series' own units.\nWhen omitted, the value of the slot immediately before the suffix is\nthe base.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "rate"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "d_22985de49498160e6347": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Currency-tagged monetary amount with safe arithmetic.\n\nValues retain decimal precision independently of ISO 4217 display precision.\n\nWhen you need configurable rounding during ingestion, use\n[`Money::new_with_config`].\n\n# Examples\n```rust\nuse finstack_quant_core::money::Money;\nuse finstack_quant_core::currency::Currency;\n\nlet notional = Money::from((1_000_000_i64, Currency::EUR));\nassert_eq!(notional.currency(), Currency::EUR);\nassert_eq!(notional.amount(), 1_000_000.0);\n```",
      "properties": {
        "amount": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/d_80f981bb0b9a5ed597d5",
          "description": "Monetary amount, carried on the wire as an exact decimal string rather\nthan a JSON number so no precision is lost in transit. Construction with\nconfiguration applies the selected ingest scale; raw construction does not."
        },
        "currency": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/d_8ec1251bb71584ad7eda",
          "description": "ISO 4217 currency of `amount`. Arithmetic between two `Money` values\nrequires this to match; there is no implicit conversion."
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "amount",
        "currency"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "d_23aac388db4697418a04": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Parameters of [`ForecastSpec::Override`].",
      "properties": {
        "max": {
          "description": "Upper bound clamped onto generated values, in the line's base units.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "min": {
          "description": "Lower bound clamped onto generated values, in the line's base units.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "overrides": {
          "additionalProperties": {
            "format": "double",
            "type": "number"
          },
          "description": "Exact levels by period id, in the line's base units; other periods carry forward.",
          "type": "object"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "overrides"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "d_37bdaa203daeacc7cf76": {
      "description": "Seasonal decomposition mode.",
      "oneOf": [
        {
          "const": "additive",
          "description": "Additive seasonality: Y = Trend + Seasonal + Error",
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "const": "multiplicative",
          "description": "Multiplicative seasonality: Y = Trend * Seasonal * Error",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ]
    },
    "d_39fe593d8e226e27da6a": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/d_22985de49498160e6347",
          "description": "Currency-aware amount"
        },
        {
          "description": "Unitless scalar (ratio, percentage, count, etc.)",
          "format": "double",
          "type": "number"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Value that can be currency-aware or unitless.\n\nUsed for node values that can represent:\n- **Amount**: Currency-aware monetary values (e.g., USD 1,000,000)\n- **Scalar**: Unitless values (e.g., ratios, percentages, counts)"
    },
    "d_64bfae777a8ae7e8ab2b": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Parameters of [`ForecastSpec::TimeSeries`].",
      "properties": {
        "alpha": {
          "description": "Level smoothing in (0, 1]; required for the exponential method.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "beta": {
          "description": "Trend smoothing in (0, 1]; required for the exponential method.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "historical": {
          "description": "Observations in the line's base units, oldest first.",
          "items": {
            "format": "double",
            "type": "number"
          },
          "type": "array"
        },
        "max": {
          "description": "Upper bound clamped onto generated values, in the line's base units.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "method": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/d_f59b39c1dff118611478",
          "description": "Trend model; defaults to linear."
        },
        "min": {
          "description": "Lower bound clamped onto generated values, in the line's base units.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "phi": {
          "description": "Trend damping in (0, 1]; legal only with the exponential method.",
          "format": "double",
          "type": [
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "window": {
          "description": "Averaging window in periods; required for the moving-average method.",
          "format": "uint64",
          "minimum": 0,
          "type": [
            "integer",
            "null"
          ]
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "historical",
        "method"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
    "d_80f981bb0b9a5ed597d5": {
      "description": "Exact decimal encoded only as a JSON string.\n\nRestoration routes through [`crate::decimal::parse_decimal`], the single\nexact text-admission rule: JSON numbers, malformed text and inexact values\nare rejected rather than rounded. Serialization writes canonical\nfixed-point text with trailing zeros removed and signed zero normalized\n(`\"1.5\"`, `\"0\"`), never scientific notation.",
      "pattern": "^[+-]?(?:[0-9]+(?:\\.[0-9]*)?|\\.[0-9]+)(?:[eE][+-]?[0-9]+)?$",
      "type": "string"
    },
